WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
Good day, good people, how are you, what are you up to?

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to another video.

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Look here, bro.

4
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:19.250
Not such a big miss, bro.

5
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:26.490
So, today I want to tell you something I'm very proud of.

6
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.490
I'm very happy about it, folks.

7
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.390
Thank you first of all for hitting "subscribe."

8
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:38.970
Second, because it's in a sense a confirmation that I'm not a complete fool, not totally crazy,

9
00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.790
but that I can say something cool, interesting, or at least am interesting myself.

10
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.710
And you know what, there's something else. Do you know that since corona began...

11
00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:55.210
I think this corona period essentially began a year ago, 27.04,

12
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.250
because that's when they let us work a little.

13
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:05.790
And during this period I created, besides a YouTube channel for 20,000 of you,

14
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.570
one more gym, and, well, almost made one more café.

15
00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:18.630
So I'm, in short, proud of all this, when I rewind a year back

16
00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:22.490
and understand that it's a very good foundation for the future.

17
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:37.110
By the way, of course, naturally, on the occasion of the number 20,000 here and 30,000 on Instagram

18
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.350
I'm preparing a bigger giveaway for you.

19
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.810
That is, I want there to be several prizes, for lots of people to take part

20
00:01:43.810 --> 00:02:03.010
and, of course, above all, for people to win prizes,

21
00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.630
so that something's rolling, you understand.

22
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.810
Now I'm heading to Vračar, I need to hand out salaries,

23
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.070
and last month I blew a pile of cash at Vračar

24
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.890
on these repairs, finishing, buying materials and all that,

25
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.330
so right now there's complete chaos there, which doesn't usually happen,

26
00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.410
because my brother Dare keeps track of it like no one else,

27
00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.170
it's literally known where every dinar went,

28
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:29.930
but right now, at the moment, again it's known, but there's no cash,

29
00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.050
because I spent it all on this renovation,

30
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.030
so we'll go take a look at the construction site,

31
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.630
you've practically not seen it for a while,

32
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.870
I deliberately don't film all the time so the change is visible.

33
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:52.520
So, the door is installed, see this door, it's not a door but a powerhouse,

34
00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.000
when the Grind logo goes here, it'll be a bomb.

35
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.800
We have the floor, that is, the screed is fully ready,

36
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.380
everything's level, the toilet is ready for installing everything,

37
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.160
don't let that surprise you, because the cistern is built in,

38
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.960
there'll be a shelf here, here I'll sell, bro, the coffee of a lifetime,

39
00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:15.340
that is, here will be the best part, here: glass shelves, a windowsill to sit on,

40
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.020
walls, ceiling, there'll be pendant lights, you see how many windows, and that's it.

41
00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:22.920
Here will be the bar counter,

42
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.600
that is, from this protrusion the counter runs,

43
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.400
all this will be the counter, and here the magic will be born.

44
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.160
They say the counter is the most important part of a café,

45
00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.180
because it makes you money, that's the pure truth,

46
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:40.560
but here the most important part of the establishment is not inside but outside,

47
00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.100
you'll see now, right here.

48
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.840
Seriously, right? Look.

49
00:03:52.100 --> 00:04:01.000
There, folks, we've come to two key weeks,

50
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.380
that is, now we need to tidy these pallets a bit,

51
00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.360
we need to insert slats between them to even everything out,

52
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.060
varnish, plane and so on.

53
00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:14.620
Inside the establishment, when we put in the counter — it's the most important thing for us —

54
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.580
we'll start training people,

55
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:22.100
we'll start carefully painting and furnishing with all sorts of little things, and that's all.

56
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.540
We believe that by May 15 we'll finish everything,

57
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:31.100
that the coffee for both the filter and the Turkish pot, and, of course, for espresso will be ready,

58
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.200
for espresso it's already ready, so basically we're ready,

59
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.900
and I think a wonderful, wonderful summer awaits us here.

60
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:44.080
As it does all of you who are near Vračar or just want to come to Vračar,

61
00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.360
to sit on this wonderful terrace or try Grind coffee.

62
00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.460
This part is left to finish, we're being let down a bit by these grates,

63
00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.580
let down a bit by the level of the pallets, which because of the terrace had to be made like this.

64
00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.080
Here, so, it would reach the middle of the door,

65
00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.900
but basically, when we lay artificial grass here on the right

66
00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:08.120
and make some planters here, something to sit on and so on,

67
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:13.200
it will be something between "Belgrade on the Water" and Barcelona.

68
00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.860
I wonder what the team is doing in the gym.

69
00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.000
At "First Team" the morning workouts have ended.

70
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:24.080
Good afternoon. This is what the Grind logo will look like, just look, dear bro.

71
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:30.500
The LED strip shines here and lights up the black wall as if it were on fire.

72
00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:36.200
Morning workouts are over, so there's utter idleness here, though no, Sarica is working out a bit.

73
00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.840
Yes, yes, hi, Sarica.

74
00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.360
You keep training, girls.

75
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:07.220
So, folks, I'm back in the city, first to grab two coffees and pour them into myself,

76
00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.520
because I haven't had a single one since morning.

77
00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.740
Well, it often happens that I don't drink coffee in the morning,

78
00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:18.000
but brain fog like this doesn't happen often, bro, I'm dull as a post.

79
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Today I can't string together a simple sentence,

80
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.920
so I'll knock back two, three, five-six coffees — that'll be the thing.

81
00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:29.360
Kidding, not five-six, bro, two, and that's enough, I don't need more.

82
00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:42.400
I understand that in the city sometimes you can park somewhere and sometimes you can't,

83
00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.820
but, bro, I don't understand when some cars chase me to film every mistake of mine,

84
00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.620
and there's no mistake at all — that I don't understand.

85
00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:57.920
At last the knowledge and skill will pass, bro, to some other young people, right?

86
00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:04.000
Folks, the house of good coffee: here, at "Pržionica," I learned what good coffee is,

87
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.200
and I won't annoy you much with the camera here,

88
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.320
but in any case, if you need a good coffee in this city, this is the very place.

89
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.280
Thanks, bro!

90
00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.520
So, said hello to the guys, I may have lingered a bit.

91
00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:39.600
Look, a completely altered state of consciousness and mind after two coffees, after a good conversation,

92
00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.340
and I bought myself a coffee.

93
00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.440
They really are, I think, coffee champions, I think there's none better than them,

94
00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:52.020
so if you're in the city and want good coffee, definitely: Kralja Petra street, see where I am?

95
00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:57.760
You surely see, next to the "Suvobor" kafana.

96
00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:03.560
And, of course, since everything begins and ends at "First Team," elite Belgrade fitness,

97
00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.200
now we're waiting here for Kinez, to tour the city

98
00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:12.420
and comment a bit on the best spots for street workout and outdoor training in general,

99
00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.940
maybe do something and so on.

100
00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:16.740
That's it, bro, let's go!

101
00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.860
Since a deal is a deal, bro, we first stopped to write down where we're going,

102
00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.660
instead of setting off and deciding along the way.

103
00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:47.510
So, let's go, friends, and our first stop is in about three minutes.

104
00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.860
It's probably the biggest and best-known spot in Belgrade and definitely a spot...

105
00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:58.860
In Serbia, the most popular in Serbia.

106
00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:05.080
Kind of, yes, and definitely the spot where Back to the Basics and the most popular guys film almost all

107
00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.840
of their big videos, unless, of course, in Obrenovac.

108
00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.120
Let's take a look at what this spot offers.

109
00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:35.100
It's time to comment a bit, give a rating,

110
00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.340
and since I, bro, don't know exactly what to say —

111
00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.160
it's street workout, after all — first I'll give the floor to Kinez,

112
00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.300
so we listen to the bro, let him explain everything bit by bit and say what he thinks.

113
00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:49.000
So, the first thing we see when we arrive at the spot is this pull-up apparatus,

114
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.280
that is, we have one high bar, one a bit lower.

115
00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:55.080
As for the thickness of the bar, which is probably the most important thing when it comes to pull-ups,

116
00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.080
in my opinion for my hand it should be slightly bigger.

117
00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.260
Probably Vuk would agree, his hands are even bigger,

118
00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.800
for those with smaller ones it may suit, but that's how it is.

119
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.860
And as for the other apparatus, we have three sets of parallel bars for dips,

120
00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:12.220
in my experience, I trained here a lot,

121
00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.100
those in the middle are the best,

122
00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:19.620
so if you come here, to Tašmajdan Park, pick them and do dips on them.

123
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.480
A neutral-grip pull-up bar, or rather a monkey bar,

124
00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.140
well, basically it's not bad, only one could

125
00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:34.960
reproach it that it's a bit low and that the distances between these bars are a bit narrow,

126
00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.000
but it's nothing terrible, I mostly did these neutral-grip pull-ups on it.

127
00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:45.360
If we talk about the type of workout: if you do supersets — pull-up, dips, push-ups or something like that —

128
00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.860
here it's really quite good, because you don't have to walk much.

129
00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.460
If you pull up on the monkey bar, the parallel bars are right next to it,

130
00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.220
if on this regular bar — there are these lower parallel bars, so that's not bad either.

131
00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.320
But if you combine with skull crushers or triceps extensions,

132
00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.840
there may be a small problem, because the distance is greater.

133
00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.960
Now Vuk will give his opinion, and then...

134
00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:04.940
And first you give a rating.

135
00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:09.200
Overall, I wouldn't say about any spot I've seen in Serbia that it's a 10,

136
00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.460
but this one would be about a seven and a half to an eight.

137
00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.640
Okay, let it be an 8, since I've spent a lot of time here, purely for subjective reasons.

138
00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.740
Well, folks, what can I say about this spot?

139
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.800
First of all — I'm missing something to work the legs with.

140
00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.460
After all, bro, legs are half the body, you know the story.

141
00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:29.860
I'd put some huge rock here or just concrete something onto a barbell,

142
00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.280
especially as there's room to place it.

143
00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.920
So if anyone has an idea and spends their life here, that's great.

144
00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.700
I notice the pull-up bars are covered in plastic.

145
00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:41.040
I like to coat them with paint mixed with sand,

146
00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.600
because then they don't slip.

147
00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.880
On the other hand, I know these bars are slippery, and street workout athletes solve it with sponges.

148
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.340
But again, in my opinion, this isn't very good:

149
00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.360
it needs maintenance, bro, painting, upkeep.

150
00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:58.200
As for equipment, we have everything needed for pull-ups and dips.

151
00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.940
There's a flat area, there's tartan to train on.

152
00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:06.180
I'd give this spot a 7, because it works only half of the body.

153
00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:07.060
On we go.

154
00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:11.700
And as we leave Tašmajdan Park, let's just sum up.

155
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.040
So, Tašmajdan Park is perhaps the best place to train.

156
00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.840
Our ratings — 7 and 8.

157
00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.140
We're very lucky that the city is empty.

158
00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:27.920
Because at five we actually have to go to New Belgrade and push through the biggest traffic jams.

159
00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:32.940
Fortunately there's nobody around, tomorrow is May 1 already, so we're relaxed.

160
00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:40.180
Those who know, know, and for those who don't — we'll explain now.

161
00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.520
Here we are at "Olimp," that is, the Zvezdara temple of sport.

162
00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.280
We came to see a serious place to train.

163
00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.280
You'll see now.

164
00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:00.740
This is probably for rings or for hanging something.

165
00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.660
The parallel bars are good, huh? And this is for the "dragon flag."

166
00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:09.170
And this is a very interesting apparatus.

167
00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:13.430
I don't know whether it was made for that, but basically you can do a hyperextension hold on it.

168
00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.090
The Sorensen hold, this is really good.

169
00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:17.610
A big plus for this spot.

170
00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:23.830
Well, looking: what we were just talking about, the distance from the bar to the parallel bars — here it's quite small.

171
00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:25.550
But maybe it'd be better if they were a bit narrower.

172
00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:28.990
They seem wide to me, yes.

173
00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:29.730
Well, a bit wide.

174
00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.430
These pull-ups: excellent height and an excellent bar.

175
00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:35.110
What you were saying about the plastic coating isn't here.

176
00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.710
Yes, it's paint with sand.

177
00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.630
There's a monkey bar, and it's perfect.

178
00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:40.570
In my opinion this is the best monkey bar.

179
00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:48.110
Overall, the space is used as economically as possible, and that's a plus for training efficiency.

180
00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:49.790
There are additional apparatus here too.

181
00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:54.850
Say, if I were chasing dips like last year, I'd definitely do them on that apparatus over there.

182
00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.270
Because there the height is good, everything everything is perfect.

183
00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:01.230
If I were doing a circuit workout, I'd do dips here.

184
00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.670
So I have such an alternative too.

185
00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:06.370
There's that log over there on which I'd do incline and decline push-ups.

186
00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:10.750
As for the second half of the body, Vuk will surely mention it.

187
00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:14.070
Again the same problem, which I wouldn't even consider a problem.

188
00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:17.410
Well, you can split this into two different workouts.

189
00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.070
And there are additional apparatus here too, like this one for the Sorensen hold.

190
00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.190
You just said that.

191
00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:28.990
And for skull crushers a pile of apparatus, for incline push-ups — in short, everything there is.

192
00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.070
Basically a very, very good spot.

193
00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.510
I'd say it's better than Taš, because here nothing is scattered at all.

194
00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.210
This spot — eight and a half.

195
00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:41.210
As for me, I like this spot much more than the previous one.

196
00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.890
What I like here most of all: you can see it's looked after, bro.

197
00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:48.050
You can see someone paints it, you can see someone is working,

198
00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.850
and didn't just take the money from a tender, bro, and pour plastic over everything.

199
00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:53.670
I have a bit of a businesslike attitude to all this.

200
00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.490
What else I like: well, this Sorensen hold, we said it's fire.

201
00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.190
There's a bench that can be used for jumping up.

202
00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.050
Yes, yes, or for lounging around.

203
00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.650
Or for lounging around. There are two or three parallel bars.

204
00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.930
There's a log, bro, for walking, if we're in the mood.

205
00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.070
There's tartan for running, that's very good.

206
00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:16.330
Here we can, of course, do everything on this tartan, we can do something for the legs.

207
00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:17.890
There's a huge rock, bro.

208
00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:21.210
Some don't know what it's for, and some do, bro,

209
00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:24.010
that it's basically for doing goblet squats and that sort of thing.

210
00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.290
I believe that's what it's for.

211
00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.910
So from me too the rating here is eight and a half.

212
00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.250
So on average eight and a half.

213
00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:32.430
Serious stuff.

214
00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.320
I didn't even know about this place, never trained here.

215
00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.000
But, bro, look what a forest.

216
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.620
It gets a plus 1 just for the forest.

217
00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:51.440
I think the apparatus isn't that good, but it is what it is.

218
00:15:51.440 --> 00:16:10.850
You need to take a barbell and concrete the ends.

219
00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.010
Like that, a bit of deadlift.

220
00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.610
For everyone, bro, for the broad masses: the deadlift.

221
00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.390
It could be a front squat, it could be a back squat with a barbell.

222
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:26.310
Well, yes, there could be some lunges.

223
00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.890
Let's take a look, bro, you found yourself a toy, huh, bro?

224
00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:45.780
Checkmate.

225
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.200
And what do you say about this kind of setup?

226
00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:56.420
A completely different story.

227
00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.560
I like this place the most,

228
00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:05.900
because it's in the dense shade of the Zvezdara forest.

229
00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.040
Serious stuff.

230
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.880
You can run wherever you like,

231
00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:11.620
because there are as many of these dirt paths as you want.

232
00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.760
Not too hard, pleasant.

233
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:19.180
As for the apparatus, as I predicted with pessimistic forecasts at the start,

234
00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.200
everything is a bit scuffed, a bit cracked,

235
00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.850
but, bro, here you can simply do real hardcore.

236
00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:26.770
What I like very much here

237
00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:30.570
is that there's weight you can use to do squats, lunges and all that.

238
00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:31.610
There's that stump over there.

239
00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:32.810
See the big stump here?

240
00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.490
You can hug the big stump and do anything.

241
00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.150
You can do a "pistol" squat sitting down on the stump.

242
00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:41.430
And as for pull-ups, dips and everything else,

243
00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.890
you can manage, it can all be fine.

244
00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:46.630
You keep talking about legs, as if we're at a gym.

245
00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:52.210
Okay, pull-ups, parallel bars — that goes without saying, as do all the prison exercises, push-ups.

246
00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:56.750
It's really great for training here, and for anyone close to Zvezdara it's definitely worth coming.

247
00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.770
Considering I gave "Olimp" an eight and a half, here it's an eight.

248
00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:04.730
Well, with what Vuk said, I mostly agree.

249
00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:08.570
The problem for me was these parallel bars for dips,

250
00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:12.650
because they were too low, and I trained right here when I was chasing rep counts.

251
00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:16.770
And basically, if high — it gets in the way because I jump up, if low — it gets in the way because I have to bend my legs.

252
00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.690
So the ones at "Olimp" were the most ideal for me.

253
00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.650
There, that's a certain minus of this spot.

254
00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.950
And what's also a big plus is the monkey bar.

255
00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.910
What I said about "Olimp," I'd say the same here.

256
00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:30.790
The height is good, in my opinion, and those who are shorter will have to jump.

257
00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.710
For me it was perfect.

258
00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:35.010
And as for the bars themselves — they basically don't slip.

259
00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.390
What Vuk said — they add sand.

260
00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.790
And what else should we comment on?

261
00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:45.830
What we haven't seen before are these two low bars.

262
00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.350
Like inclined parallel bars.

263
00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:50.390
Here you can practice the impossible dip.

264
00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:52.910
That is, do these "impossible dips."

265
00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:59.550
And you can do incline push-ups or put your feet on this stump.

266
00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:03.450
And that's exactly the place where I did 300 push-ups at the end of a pushing workout.

267
00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.030
That is, feet on the stump — and you pump out push-ups.

268
00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.630
And as for the rating, I'd agree with Vuk.

269
00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:09.790
So let it be an eight.

270
00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:12.050
It would be a clean ten if the parallel bars were better.

271
00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:12.770
On to the next.

272
00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.930
We stopped in for a bite to eat,

273
00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.930
so we don't keel over before evening.

274
00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:20.950
And we hope we'll manage to visit everything before it gets dark.

275
00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:21.730
What can I tell you?

276
00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:29.110
Folks, I, as an old Vračar native, just told Kinez one thing.

277
00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.630
I can tell you too.

278
00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:31.710
Kinez says it's interesting.

279
00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.010
You see this building behind me.

280
00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:35.610
This is what Vračar was like when I was a kid.

281
00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:37.270
In this kind of Vračar I lived.

282
00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.970
And, basically, we played football between a pole and the corner of a building.

283
00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:41.770
Those were the goals.

284
00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.690
And now Vračar is like this.

285
00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:48.130
I don't know whether that's good or bad.

286
00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.850
We agreed not to divide things into good and bad.

287
00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.070
And here we are at Košutnjak, folks.

288
00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:57.110
It was long overdue to come here.

289
00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.170
And here people are celebrating May Day.

290
00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.650
People are marking Good Friday.

291
00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:05.470
Marking the day before May Day and three days before Easter.

292
00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:08.570
That's quite an attractive holiday right now.

293
00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:15.090
And besides, we've come to yet another of the best places to train in the city,

294
00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:20.210
which is also new and also has orange as its basic color.

295
00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.290
Look here.

296
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.600
You'll see now.

297
00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:30.460
Kinez and I realized that we've actually never run here.

298
00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.620
I run sometimes, but not that much, you know.

299
00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.660
I wore this track out while playing basketball.

300
00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.460
So since then I had one summer when I ran.

301
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.160
Everything else was occasional.

302
00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.940
Anyway, this training spot...

303
00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.580
Yes, specific.

304
00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.160
How did he say it, specific?

305
00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:57.680
The specifics of this spot is that it's more for amateurs who want to fit pull-ups and parallel bars

306
00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.020
into a running workout.

307
00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:03.220
So we'll explain that to you in more detail too, and now let's walk around a bit.

308
00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.400
There, we're going now.

309
00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:07.000
Whether we'll do a lap or not isn't clear to us yet.

310
00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.760
But here, for example, an incline bench with a double bar.

311
00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:10.780
It's located here.

312
00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:12.080
See what it looks like.

313
00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:15.920
Anyway, there's a one-kilometer track here,

314
00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:21.100
and every, say, 200 meters there's an exercise corner,

315
00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:24.280
and there's everything, even in several variants.

316
00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:28.120
So here you can set yourself up a great interval workout:

317
00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:31.940
for example, run a bit, then do some exercise and so on.

318
00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:33.520
I think this is really good.

319
00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:37.080
Besides, it's the cleanest air in Belgrade, that's really serious.

320
00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:38.380
This is really CrossFit style.

321
00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.550
Come on, do the same thing in slow motion.

322
00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:50.670
That was too fast, I don't know whether the camera has that many frames.

323
00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:53.690
And these are real parallel bars, bro, cool.

324
00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:12.370
Here, then, is another point, after 200 meters.

325
00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:16.050
And again it's a multifunctional apparatus.

326
00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:27.790
And here they are, these old apparatus for pull-ups and dips.

327
00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:32.170
And we also have here, well yes, this "vaulting horse."

328
00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:34.030
Here, basically, is the center of events.

329
00:22:34.030 --> 00:22:36.050
It's the center of events, bro.

330
00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:48.190
Well, anyway, what you were talking about can be done.

331
00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:52.450
Do any workout, any kind of supersets and everything else.

332
00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:56.430
Let's go now to the first position, deliver our verdict and ratings, okay?

333
00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:59.910
Oh, here's an interesting spot.

334
00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:03.230
What do you say, a point higher for this, huh?

335
00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:10.050
Give us one in slow motion, bro.

336
00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:33.010
Among all this good stuff for training we found something that's good for almost nothing, bro.

337
00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:37.290
You tie your shoelaces here.

338
00:23:37.910 --> 00:23:39.310
You tie your shoelaces here.

339
00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.630
There, here the width is good, the height is good, all that.

340
00:23:42.790 --> 00:23:44.190
Now this is a different matter, bro.

341
00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:48.810
Here's another station with little benches.

342
00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:54.570
That is, you can jump up on them, you can do split squats.

343
00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:55.030
Stretch.

344
00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:57.290
And you can stretch too, yes, of course.

345
00:23:57.430 --> 00:24:00.110
Although this isn't part of the spot, the guys brought it.

346
00:24:03.530 --> 00:24:07.150
Too bad it doesn't stay in the forest, someone should hang some wooden rings.

347
00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.950
And here's my recommendation to everyone who likes to train outdoors,

348
00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:14.430
who likes to train in nature and who is constantly on the move:

349
00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:19.250
have rings, have a resistance band for yourself, a kettlebell or adjustable dumbbells,

350
00:24:19.250 --> 00:24:21.730
a good jump rope and one more thing.

351
00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:22.390
A good attitude.

352
00:24:22.590 --> 00:24:24.270
Take a good attitude with you.

353
00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:40.140
You know what, we've reached the end of this loop,

354
00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:44.080
and, honestly, it was a bit chaotic, because we didn't know what to expect.

355
00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:48.280
We didn't even expect to go the whole loop, and Kinez at some point says: let's go around the loop.

356
00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:49.920
At some point he starts running.

357
00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:52.560
Well, you've got to run a bit too.

358
00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:54.320
But here, we've gone around the whole loop.

359
00:24:54.460 --> 00:24:59.380
A big plus, looking at it overall, because there are many apparatus in many places,

360
00:24:59.380 --> 00:25:01.460
that is, if there's a crowd somewhere, you can go to another place.

361
00:25:01.620 --> 00:25:04.640
And for everything that could possibly come to mind — a plus.

362
00:25:04.940 --> 00:25:06.080
Everything, absolutely everything.

363
00:25:06.160 --> 00:25:10.560
Well, a minus can be given for what you said: covered in plastic, slippery.

364
00:25:10.780 --> 00:25:13.180
Okay, we put sponges on, so it's not that bad.

365
00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:20.440
But the main shortcoming of this spot is that there's no bar with parallel bars next to it for dips.

366
00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:25.040
That is, if we want to do a superset, this kind of workout is impossible here.

367
00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:29.240
Except straight bar dips, that is, dips on a straight bar — that can be done.

368
00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:32.660
That would be my solution if I were training here.

369
00:25:33.220 --> 00:25:37.160
So, looking at it, it's not such a minus that I wouldn't give this spot a nine.

370
00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:39.260
I'm also for a nine, folks.

371
00:25:39.260 --> 00:25:43.440
First, because it's a temple of sport and the best air in Belgrade is here.

372
00:25:43.560 --> 00:25:46.140
Second, because this running track is so well made.

373
00:25:46.360 --> 00:25:52.160
I used to run on asphalt here first, then on sawdust, and now there's tartan here — and I don't run anymore.

374
00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:56.800
Kidding, it's not that I don't run, but it's not that I pick it as my main activity either.

375
00:25:56.800 --> 00:25:59.980
But in any case — an excellent one-kilometer track,

376
00:25:59.980 --> 00:26:02.560
you can test yourself, calmly run a half marathon here,

377
00:26:02.560 --> 00:26:04.520
and you won't be bored, because it's beautiful.

378
00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:09.600
Lots of people, good energy, you saw the guys with rings and everything else.

379
00:26:12.860 --> 00:26:16.060
Kinez says: yes, there's no superset of parallel bars and pull-ups,

380
00:26:16.060 --> 00:26:19.480
but push-ups and pull-ups or handstand push-ups and pull-ups can be done.

381
00:26:19.480 --> 00:26:20.820
So that's okay.

382
00:26:20.820 --> 00:26:24.700
There are things that can be used for working on the legs,

383
00:26:24.700 --> 00:26:27.500
like all sorts of benches you can jump up on,

384
00:26:27.500 --> 00:26:30.720
and you can do "pistols," helping yourself to sit down.

385
00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:34.860
There are things you can carry — rocks and everything else people brought.

386
00:26:34.940 --> 00:26:37.140
There are new apparatus, there are old apparatus.

387
00:26:37.200 --> 00:26:43.420
What I don't like — such spots are usually built by people who understand nothing about it.

388
00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:51.060
And in the end they just do a lot of things wrong, lots of useless apparatus and all that.

389
00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:55.600
On the other hand, if they had asked someone like us, who've been using this for years —

390
00:26:55.600 --> 00:27:00.820
everything could be much better, higher quality, and the finishing could be better.

391
00:27:00.820 --> 00:27:05.100
Well, some tanks drove by, planes flew over, so we waited it out a bit, helicopters.

392
00:27:05.180 --> 00:27:09.320
Anyway, in my opinion — and I see my bro thinks the same —

393
00:27:09.320 --> 00:27:12.040
this is the best place to train in our city.

394
00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:16.860
And in my opinion, now that I've gone around this kilometer loop — there's another station.

395
00:27:16.960 --> 00:27:22.140
That is, we skipped one, but I think we filmed everything for you. To me it's a clean nine.

396
00:27:26.220 --> 00:27:30.260
But a nine it is. That's it, folks, we're heading to our final point,

397
00:27:30.260 --> 00:27:34.480
some may guess where it is, some have no idea — they'll find out now.

398
00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:43.430
We're back home, at least to my home. Like that. There it is, that very spot.

399
00:27:43.870 --> 00:27:47.870
Maybe there are better-equipped spots, maybe some are more beautiful,

400
00:27:47.870 --> 00:27:49.850
but this one is probably the best, right, bro?

401
00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:53.710
Yes, yes, yes. That's what you say. Now we'll prove it. Let's take a look.

402
00:28:00.430 --> 00:28:06.930
So, folks, we're at "25 May," you see Nole's building here, we're at Nebojša Tower.

403
00:28:07.310 --> 00:28:10.870
The confluence of two rivers, the Sava and the Danube, well start, bro.

404
00:28:10.870 --> 00:28:14.970
So. There's this bar, it stood here back then too,

405
00:28:14.970 --> 00:28:18.890
it was the same bar, and for pure pull-ups it's maybe the best of all.

406
00:28:21.920 --> 00:28:24.060
They did pull-ups on it when I could do only three.

407
00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:30.360
Here are these parallel bars, which back then were bad, because, see, how wide they are.

408
00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:41.080
So, folks, from today this is called the "dragon flag-ette."

409
00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:46.300
And then this was built up, I wasn't here for a couple of years,

410
00:28:46.300 --> 00:28:49.060
and when I came, I saw: apparently this monkey bar had appeared here.

411
00:28:54.640 --> 00:28:59.540
I saw: here, where there's this gravel and all that, new apparatus appeared, and they're very good.

412
00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:02.660
There are parallel bars here that are, one might say, ideal.

413
00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:07.400
The height and all that. This monkey bar, and the second monkey bar too, are excellent.

414
00:29:07.820 --> 00:29:12.100
The pull-up bar — well, the only thing is that there's just one, the one we've just shown.

415
00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:17.680
And here we have these two, which would be ideal, because there are two and several people can do the same thing.

416
00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:19.080
A bit thick, huh?

417
00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:22.700
Yes, their minus is precisely that it's thick, so I'd never use it.

418
00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:32.880
There's also this apparatus for push-ups, made for people two and a half meters tall.

419
00:29:58.740 --> 00:30:03.580
So, all things considered, this spot, I think, is the best in equipment.

420
00:30:03.620 --> 00:30:05.560
On the other hand, there's water nearby.

421
00:30:05.860 --> 00:30:11.360
You can zone out: after a workout sit on a bench and look at the water to relax your mind.

422
00:30:11.500 --> 00:30:13.140
The mind needs training too, not only the body.

423
00:30:19.240 --> 00:30:21.680
Yes, this one is better than the one in the Zvezdara forest.

424
00:30:21.960 --> 00:30:27.100
Yes, yes, yes, rating nine and a half out of 10, there are small shortcomings, and for me it's the best spot.

425
00:30:27.280 --> 00:30:29.540
And now my view of things, a different view of things.

426
00:30:29.800 --> 00:30:33.160
I don't know how safe it is, but I know I want to try it.

427
00:30:35.680 --> 00:30:40.940
There, for me this is an example of guys who don't seriously understand what they're doing.

428
00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:52.100
But, to make the trouble bigger, two people can work out on it.

429
00:30:55.140 --> 00:30:59.660
That is, basically it's discarded rolled metal, and the price of metal has shot up.

430
00:31:03.120 --> 00:31:07.620
And worst of all, this apparatus is the most complicated, bro, that is, the most time went into it.

431
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:08.960
And it's the least important.

432
00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:15.240
And completely unnecessary, but then people come and say: the state gave me something to work out on here,

433
00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:16.540
like now I'm going to do this.

434
00:31:30.700 --> 00:31:34.060
You know, the tire is not that light, and that's good.

435
00:31:34.220 --> 00:31:38.660
That is, I had to lift, say, about 50, 40 kilos, and that's really good.

436
00:31:39.100 --> 00:31:43.520
You can carry the tire, you can put it on yourself and squat, you can do anything.

437
00:31:43.880 --> 00:31:45.000
And that, in my opinion, is great.

438
00:31:45.280 --> 00:31:49.480
As for this pull-up bar, I agree it's thick,

439
00:31:49.660 --> 00:31:53.820
but again, for grip strength it's not so bad, plus it's quite low here,

440
00:31:53.820 --> 00:31:59.860
so the kids we saw today, and there are really many of them, who start training from this height...

441
00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:08.240
Okay, this is a real imitation of gymnastic parallel bars.

442
00:32:14.820 --> 00:32:19.760
I think for ordinary people it's really high and not too good,

443
00:32:19.820 --> 00:32:23.260
but again, bro, okay, there are different options, there's another set for dips,

444
00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:29.220
there's this one of yours for push-ups from the floor, which is great, the monkey bar, there's this weight, go to it.

445
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:32.160
I kept waiting for you to notice it.

446
00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:35.580
This weight is actually not heavier than the one in the Zvezdara forest.

447
00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:48.780
So you can do biceps too, right?

448
00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:50.040
Good stuff.

449
00:32:50.220 --> 00:32:53.240
As for this clearing, I'm very pleased with it too.

450
00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:57.920
You can run, you can do lots of things, there's a bike path.

451
00:32:58.420 --> 00:33:02.260
And so, honestly, my rating is 9, but considering that it's my neighborhood,

452
00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:07.020
considering that I love this neighborhood most of all, considering that bro Nole built something here,

453
00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:10.280
a rating of nine and a half for "25 May."

454
00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:11.180
There you go.

455
00:33:21.370 --> 00:33:26.810
If by chance this video is being watched by the handsome guy who built this,

456
00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:30.170
I can recommend that he just do something else.

457
00:33:37.490 --> 00:33:38.630
It was a good tour, huh?

458
00:33:38.710 --> 00:33:39.650
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

459
00:33:39.890 --> 00:33:44.910
So, folks, we've toured what we think is the best in this city.

460
00:33:45.130 --> 00:33:47.270
We haven't toured New Belgrade and Zemun.

461
00:33:47.570 --> 00:33:51.910
If you want us to tour New Belgrade and Zemun, write about it in the comments

462
00:33:51.910 --> 00:33:55.270
and get me up to fifteen hundred likes.

463
00:33:56.630 --> 00:34:00.330
Fifteen hundred likes is perfectly fine for videos like this,

464
00:34:00.330 --> 00:34:04.130
for us to go, that is, tour New Belgrade and Zemun.

465
00:34:04.510 --> 00:34:07.010
What we wanted to achieve with this video —

466
00:34:07.230 --> 00:34:10.350
is to stir you up a bit, broaden a bit your idea of

467
00:34:10.350 --> 00:34:14.210
where you can train at all and in what ways you can train,

468
00:34:14.210 --> 00:34:18.490
and at the same time draw your attention to what, in our opinion, is important for a spot,

469
00:34:18.970 --> 00:34:23.350
and we also hope that someone who makes decisions will see this video

470
00:34:23.350 --> 00:34:27.550
and say: well yes, let me tell the guys who handle this to build spots like these.

471
00:34:33.790 --> 00:34:36.650
Well yes, this will definitely be useful to people who come —

472
00:34:36.730 --> 00:34:40.170
say, new students or high schoolers coming from other places —

473
00:34:40.750 --> 00:34:44.450
so they know where to find good spots.

474
00:34:44.830 --> 00:34:48.790
I haven't yet met a spot of which I can say it's ideal

475
00:34:48.790 --> 00:34:52.250
in the sense that it covers absolutely everything I need,

476
00:34:52.330 --> 00:34:55.670
I have to compromise depending on the workout —

477
00:34:55.670 --> 00:34:57.290
which spot I'll go to, most often.

478
00:34:57.470 --> 00:34:58.150
That's what I do.

479
00:35:00.990 --> 00:35:03.270
Yes, and one more thing we talked about:

480
00:35:03.790 --> 00:35:06.390
if this takes off, and it may,

481
00:35:06.510 --> 00:35:08.530
we could go to other cities too,

482
00:35:08.610 --> 00:35:10.810
like Novi Sad, Niš...

483
00:35:10.810 --> 00:35:13.150
Bye, folks, we've tired you out enough with this video,

484
00:35:13.290 --> 00:35:15.130
but we believe you found it interesting.

485
00:35:16.150 --> 00:35:16.530
Novi Sad.